<title>LUXEMBOURG: Safra Q3 profit rises 18 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Safra Q3 profit rises 18 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter ended September 30</p>
<p>		    (million U.S. dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>						    Q3 96	   Q3 95</p>
<p> Group net income			     48.4     vs   41.2</p>
<p> Net per share (dollars)		     2.75    vs    2.33</p>
<p>Nine months ended Sept 30</p>
<p> Group net income			    138.6     vs  120.0</p>
<p> Net per share (dollars)		     7.87    vs    6.77</p>
<p> Total client accounts		     20,800    vs  16,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Safra Republic Holdings SA is the holding company for six private banks. Total client accounts for the 1996 quarter include client assets from Banque Unigestion SA, a Geneva-based private bank purchased in July.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
